Boost.Process 1.86 does not compile on NetBSD or OpenBSD. Backported from
upstream (boostorg/process, Boost 1.87 unless noted):
- src/ext/cmd.cpp: the NetBSD and OpenBSD cmd() return `vec`, a
  std::vector<std::string>, from a function returning `shell` ("no viable
  conversion"), and OpenBSD's calls kvm_close() on the std::unique_ptr that
  already closes it.
- src/ext/exe.cpp: NetBSD has no <alloca.h>.
- src/posix/close_handles.cpp: NetBSD/OpenBSD have no close_range(); use it on
  FreeBSD only and let the others take the portable fallback.
- include/boost/process/v2/posix/default_launcher.hpp: declare `environ` on
  OpenBSD (and DragonFly) too; their <unistd.h> does not (upstream develop).
Only those platforms' code changes; the rest compile identical sources.
--- a/libs/process/src/ext/cmd.cpp
+++ b/libs/process/src/ext/cmd.cpp
@@ -299,7 +299,6 @@
